  "Question": "Point P is rotated about the center of rotation O to obtain P′. Given \\(OP=5\\) and the angle of rotation \\(\\angle POP'=90^\\circ\\), find the square of PP′ (that is, the value of \\(PP'^2\\)).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "50",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Corresponding points are at equal distances from the center of rotation, so \\(OP'=OP=5\\). Triangle \\(POP'\\) is a right triangle, so \\(PP'^2=25+25=50\\).",
